==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*strew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|misconstruen}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|mis|construe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/mɪskənˈstɹuː/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|misconstru}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[interpret]] [[erroneously]], to [[understand]] [[incorrectly]]; to [[misunderstand]].
#* '''1975''': Paul Simon, ''50 Ways to Leave Your Lover'' from the album ''Still Crazy after All These Years''.
#*: {{...}} furthermore, I hope my meaning won’t be lost or '''misconstrued''' {{...}}

